ou.<br /> <br /> While that does make sense on some issues, the idea that older Glass Walkers don't have proteges or apprentices in other ways is weird. In more managerial/societal settings, as opposed to strictly technology ones, that logic fails completely. Also, the idea that there is not some Glass Walker version of Steve Jobs or Larry Ellison who can act as wise old men to the next generation is also quite weird.<br /> <br /> Still, at least now it is only Discouraged as opposed to Restricted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}